/// The `WIFI_MAC` block type.
///
/// The Wi-Fi MAC at DR_REG_WIFI_MAC_BASE. Known only from vendor binaries.
/// Words 0x0-0x4: Per-interface BSSID address and policy words used by scan and associated-STA receive filtering.
/// Words 0x20-0x15f0: Complete hardware-visible hal_he_init suffix after dbg_read_tx_power, including all reached leaves. It contains 163 ordered writes/RMWs plus the two multi-BSSID guard reads.
/// Words 0x40-0x44: Complete dbg_read_color_collision reads the 64-bit observed BSS-color bitmap. Its adjacent control word is the canonical WIFI_MAC_HE_INIT_PREFIX.RX_FIELD_CONTROL register. Open HE HIL observed color bit 25, threshold one and timeout 60 seconds.
/// Words 0x48-0xe04: Complete hal_he_init prefix through hal_init_tb_tx, stopping immediately before hal_init_tx_pwr. Twenty-two separate RMW edges and one final synchronization/status read.
/// Words 0x5c-0x60: Four interface-address pairs consumed by MAC receive filtering.
/// Words 0x7c-0xc70: Descriptor-walker registers recovered from complete rev0 ROM leaves and qualified with the open driver's rotating 32-entry RX ring.
/// Words 0x90-0x2000: Sparse source-qualified word views in the existing owned MMIO aperture; individual meanings and side effects remain unknown.
/// Word 0x98: Multifunction receive/CSI word. Complete mac_last_rxbuf_init sets bit 27; complete hal_init later replaces its low and second bytes through separate RMWs.
/// Word 0xa0: WDEV_RX_POWER_SAVE_CONF decoded by complete dbg_read_rx_misc. Complete hal_he_set_power_save sets the interface-zero intra-PPDU and BSS-color-check bits as the tail of hal_he_bssid_init; open associated-STA HIL read both bits set.
/// Word 0xa8: Receive-end state word returned by the complete hal_mac_rx_get_end_state and hal_mac_rx_get_end_info leaves.
/// Words 0xd8-0xf4: Four WDEVRX_ABORT receive-queue policy words. Complete dbg_read_rx_misc names every used bit through 19; queue three is also the complete promiscuous-sniffer control word.
/// Words 0xfc-0xca0: Eighteen direct fresh-read RMW edges before the first external HE callback in complete mac_txrx_init; complete hal_init later repeats the bit-28 set edge.
/// Word 0x110: Canonical WDEVRXCTR_BSSIDLIST word. Complete dbg_read_rx_misc names bits 19:18 RXCTL9_BSSID_POS; the HE init prefix independently writes encoding two to that same field.
/// Word 0x11c: The CSI dump configuration word beside the RX descriptor walker, at the same base.
/// Words 0x120-0x15c: Six three-word last-RX-buffer entries and their shared two-edge enable control, recovered from the complete mac_last_rxbuf_init leaf.
/// Words 0x178-0x1538: Block-ack registers of the Wi-Fi MAC beside the RX descriptor walker, at the same base: the per-queue TX block-ack state, the RX block-ack agreement update and the extra soft-AP RX block-ack entry.
/// Words 0x29c-0x2ac: Complete dbg_read_internal_txba reads one internal WDEVTXBA result: a 64-bit bitmap, two transmitter-address words and a combined fragment/starting-sequence/TID word.
/// Words 0x2b0-0x11ac: Complete hal_attenna_init transaction. The misspelled vendor symbol first visits eight reverse-stride queue/vector words, then updates one common word.
/// Word 0x2b4: Station beacon-filter control word recovered from the complete enable and disable leaves. The three low bits select beacon filtering, broadcast wakeup and unicast wakeup.
/// Words 0x2fc-0xddc: Complete COEX/PTI tail of hal_init and complete setter leaves. PTI values remain platform-supplied because the coexistence table may be changed at runtime.
/// Word 0x300: Full beacon-IE CRC/result word returned through the caller output pointer by complete hal_beacon_ie_crc_get.
/// Words 0x308-0xca8: Eight Wi-Fi-owned direct fresh-read RMW edges after the three external HE callbacks in complete mac_txrx_init. The ninth edge reaches the independently shared physical word at 0x20104C24 and is modeled by SHARED_RADIO_INIT_CONTROL.
/// Words 0x30c-0x39c: Sparse RX hardware statistics decoded by complete dbg_read_rx_count. Ten-bit and sixteen-bit masks, the signed CFO transform and every register address below follow the complete instruction body and its pinned format string. Open HE HIL observed coherent MPDU/end/data, CFO, FCS, power-drop, HT-SIG, HE-SIG-A and interrupt counts while all buffer/FIFO/TKIP counters remained zero.
/// Words 0x3a0-0x3a4: Hardware counters read by the complete hal_he_get_rx_trigger_cnt, hal_he_get_tb_times_cnt and hal_he_get_tb_qosnull_cnt leaves. These counters distinguish Trigger reception from actual trigger-based transmission and appended QoS Null responses. An ordinary controlled HE SU AP produced no Trigger frames, so all three remained zero during sustained HE DCM A-MPDU traffic.
/// Words 0x3b4-0xe64: Complete libpp.a[pp_debug.o]::dbg_lmac_diag_statis_dump ties the blob's diag0 through diag12 and diagsel labels to these sparse MMIO words. The non-contiguous geometry and absence of diag11 are properties of the complete body. Higher-level meanings and internal bit widths remain unknown.
/// Word 0x400: Frequency-memory, hardware channel-switch, NRX and channel-bandwidth registers recovered from complete finite ROM/blob bodies. Names retain UNKNOWN where the instructions prove a field but not its electrical meaning. One physical word has one identity even when a bit has different mode-dependent roles.
/// Words 0x408-0x440: Complete hal_init_tx_pwr consumes 43 two-byte PHY power results, then complete TB, immediate-response and TB-RU leaves publish 56 ordered fresh-read RMW edges. Runtime partial-RU get/set APIs select the same packed fields by the raw Trigger RU allocation. Values are PHY gain-table indices, not dBm.
/// Words 0x44c-0xc58: Hardware effects of the three HE callbacks between the direct mac_txrx_init prefix and suffix. Diagnostic logging calls are intentionally omitted.
/// Word 0x48c: PHY/baseband configuration registers recovered from complete rev0 ROM bodies and complete pinned libphy leaves. Operation-derived fields keep UNKNOWN where neither public documentation nor an independent symbol establishes the electrical meaning.
/// Words 0x4f4-0x500: Four read-only hardware result words decoded by complete dbg_read_axtb_diag and its four complete getter leaves. The names come from the pinned blob's own format strings; no field meaning is inferred from reset images. All four words remained zero when the controlled AP sent no Trigger frames.
/// Words 0x508-0x52c: Ten hardware diagnostic words decoded by complete dbg_read_ax_diag. The blob explicitly warns that these words are not latched and can be updated by a following RX frame; consume them only as best-effort diagnostics adjacent to a known Trigger reception.
/// Words 0x800-0x814: Per-interface hardware-crypto controls, shared policy mask and key validity bitmap recovered from complete libpp hal_crypto leaves.
/// Word 0xc00: Shared MAC enable gate recovered from the complete hal_enable_mac and hal_disable_mac leaves. The four individual disable-bit meanings are not independently known.
/// Word 0xc24: One physical radio word independently reached by Wi-Fi MAC initialization and Bluetooth receive setup. The owner is protocol-neutral because the two consumers update disjoint fields through fresh-read RMW operations; the name records the observed setup context without assigning an undocumented electrical meaning.
/// Words 0xc40-0xc4c: Wi-Fi MAC interrupt mask, masked status and write-to-clear aperture. The two complete hal_mac leaves independently prove the status and clear addresses. The recovered common FIQ and cold initializer prove the event-bit mapping and mask transaction used by the open ISR.
/// Words 0xc5c-0xcbc: Shared Wi-Fi CCA, timeout and completion state used by MAC transmit queues and the PHY-owned Wi-Fi CCA gate.
/// Words 0xc64-0xe1c: Complete dbg_read_rx_count decodes two eight-bit hang counters and two full-width combined hang/panic counters. All four remained zero during the connected open HE matrix baseline.
/// Word 0xca4: WDEVTXRX_TAB three custom frame-type match and ACK-index profiles decoded by complete dbg_read_rx_misc.
/// Word 0xcac: Shared MAC run/stop control. The cold open-RX frontier publishes zero; the complete vendor channel-switch chain requests quiescence here and later restarts the no-power-save profile.
/// Words 0xd34-0xd40: Four ascending physical banks represent logical EDCA queues 3,2,1,0.
/// Words 0xd74-0xdb8: Eight interleaved hardware/software Buffer Status Report values and their shared control. Complete dbg_read_bsr_info names every exposed field. Complete hal_he_get_hw_txq_bsr independently proves the eight-byte stride and low twenty-bit hardware value. The independent blob and ROM libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_tb and rom[]::mac_tx_set_tb bodies prove the write-side scheduler interpretation: for logical queues zero through three they replace the corresponding software BSR low twenty bits with the sum of every linked frame-state halfword at offset 0x22, then OR the queue bit into CONTROL[7:0]. Complete dbg_read_tx_ppdu independently names that exact halfword msdu_len, proving that this is an original-MSDU byte sum rather than MPDU, PSDU or encoded A-MPDU length. Complete HE BlockAck response/deletion paths separately select and clear TID_BITMAP bits through hal_he_set_tid_bitmap and hal_he_clr_tid_bitmap. Open HE HIL observed TID_BITMAP=1 immediately after the successful TID0 AddBA transition while sustained DCM A-MPDU remained clean. A later rev0 HIL reproduced the complete ROM write order with a 47104-byte TID0 queue: CONTROL validity read back one while SOFTWARE_BSR already read zero. This qualifies the write-side address and validity edge but leaves the zero as a live-update/read-latch ambiguity until a real AP Trigger is observed.
/// Word 0xdbc: Four MU-EDCA timer words decoded by complete dbg_read_muedca_timer. Durations are reported by the blob in eight-TU units. Complete blob and ROM libpp[hal_mac_tx.o]::mac_tx_set_tb and rom[]::mac_tx_set_tb set ENABLE in the timer selected by the logical TX queue before publishing the Trigger queue configuration. After open HE association and TID0 AddBA, all four ordinary-SU baseline words had ENABLE=0, TIMER/CURRENT/AIFS=0 and REACHED=1; that pre-port baseline AP emitted no Trigger frame.
/// Words 0xde0-0xdfc: Cold MAC initialization request/ready handshake and the adjacent two WDEV timer targets recovered from complete ROM leaves.
/// Word 0xe00: Test-only beamforming-feedback selector written by complete esp_test_bf_set_feedback. The write transforms and selector branches are exact; the public meaning of selector values zero through sixteen is not present in the archive, so only bounded functional names are assigned.
/// Words 0xe08-0xe14: Complete libpp.a[pp_debug.o]::dbg_lmac_hw_statis_dump reads these four consecutive words and prints them as txrts, txcts, track and trcts. It then reads the already canonical RX_TX_HANG/PANIC words at 0x20104e18/1c under its shorter txhung/panic labels. The blob applies no masks; the SVD therefore preserves each word without inventing subfields.
/// Words 0xe28-0xe34: Sparse receive statistics-clear and end-result words recovered from complete hal_sniffer_rx_clr_statistics and hal_mac_rx_get_end_info leaves.
/// Words 0xe9c-0xea0: Complete hal_he_disable_obss_narrow_bw_ru writes either all ones or zero into the twenty-bit bitmap and independently sets or clears a five-bit class group and the global disable bit. The leaf name proves the aggregate disable function; individual bitmap/class identities remain approximate.
/// Words 0x1364-0x13a4: Four 0x7c-byte physical vector banks represent logical EDCA queues 3,2,1,0. The write-side Trigger-based path additionally publishes the tail of its linked MPDU-length list in the word between HE-SIG-A2 and POWER.
/// Words 0x13c8-0x13d8: Non-aliased words from four 0x7c-byte completion banks representing logical EDCA queues 3,2,1,0. AUX_A/AUX_B are canonically described by the richer TX BlockAck high-address and TX queue-information registers in WIFI_MAC_RX_DMA.
/// Words 0x1800-0x1824: Twenty-five entries of ten 32-bit words. Complete hal_crypto_clr_key_entry proves the 0x28-byte stride and all ten ordered stores; set/get leaves prove the peer/control/key layout: the peer address and control word, four words of temporal key and four words the CCMP transaction only clears.
/// Word 0x1f94: Complete esp_test_get_bfr_avgsnr reads the low byte at 0x20105f94 as stream-zero average-SNR code. Code 0x7f is a special saturated/invalid value rendered with a greater-than-or-equal prefix; every other code is converted to dB as (code + 88) / 4.
